{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://schemas.traigent.ai/analytics/correlations_problem_schema.json",
  "title": "Run Correlations Problem",
  "description": "Closed RFC 9457 problem documents of experiment_run.get_run_correlations (application/problem+json). Each definition is one status/code/type combination of the backend problem catalogue with its fixed title, detail and server-minted problem_id (first 32 hex of sha256 of the type URN); nothing the client sent is echoed. NotFoundProblem is the one closed 404 for a missing, foreign, ungranted, revoked or retired run: identical bytes in every case. BadRequestProblem is a malformed experiment_run_ref or a rejected query value (method outside pearson/spearman, min_sample outside 2..10000, an unknown or tenant-selector query parameter; validated before any lookup); the problem names no parameter and echoes no value. ServiceUnavailableProblem is the declared outcome when the correlations cannot be produced within their budget (serialized response over 1 MiB, more than 128 numeric measure dimensions or 128 numeric parameter dimensions in the run, more than 10000 scoped configuration rows, more than 256 distinct stored parameter keys across the run's configurations, a stored measure or parameter name that fails the name pattern (a control character such as a tab, or over 256 characters), deadline exhausted, or a required dependency down): the response is refused, never a partial result presented as complete. 429 and 503 may carry a Retry-After header.",
  "definitions": {
